note="# Phase42 — qualified seed30 retention and typed history/volume evidence\n\nThe ordered quality-first goal remains active at Stage1, Gate1 unknown and Stage2 not admitted. H1/mothers/Registryv12, original physics/full DR/speeds/skill predicates, single canonical writer, authority/private/finite locks, reserve and deadlines remain unchanged. No new training, policy promotion or eight-expert90 graduation is claimed.\n\nC878 and S135 now each have a genuinely qualified independent seed20260930 original N80 holdout: ascent27/27 complete and contact-confirmed, descent27/27, standing26/26 no_failure; each750 controls/6000 physics/1500 feedback/750 actor/newBPTT0. Original producer grade, actual two inner waits and independent outer Popen.wait0, complete raw-byte cache and both EX releases are qualified. These are original conditional results, not a new pooled whole-skill predicate, RM70 hardware proof or SuperMimic gain. Old seed29/D6 close/grade failure remains failed; no intent/backfill or promotion. The other qualified holdout seed remains pending.\n\nThe complete typed-C2 coupling passed a separate real TorchCPU V2 functional purpose, after preserving V1's local prelaunch seal-list/dict driver failure. Source modules and complete queue, owned identity/pointers/versions and global/private RNG remain fixed. Its17,274,671-byte synthetic component is not a full native CASE/GROUP.\n\nTyped materializer V1 actually uploaded425 sources then failed a historical SOURCE identity condition before group materialization/parent/SDK/model/resources: old B2 handoff was compared to active B4. Independent whole-source audit found exactly one history-successor selector; historical published B2 seal13 and active B4 seal21 already have separate full SourceProof identities. All old source seals/handoff/failed root remain immutable. A NEW V2 fix is SOURCE only; actual future conditions are not inferred passed.\n\nA NEW functional CPU volume purpose reused the complete B4 and C2 fixture callables once each only to materialize size, not to claim repeated old-suite independent validation. Source78, inputs, owned versions, prior profile and Python/TorchCPU RNG were unchanged; GPU/SDK/model/task-data/C/locks/parent0. Reduced synthetic indent2 CASE112,407,978 and nested GROUP130,455,062 bytes exceed the unchanged64MiB bound. The explicit LOWER_BOUND_SYNTHETIC_SERIALIZATION_NOT_FULL_NATIVE_BOUND label is not a mathematical native bound or actual native failure; full native sizes remain unknown. Source audit/design considers compact JSON while preserving all decoded data, old64MiB/16MiB limits and original scheduler/resource/close functions. No cap inflation, payload dropping, fewer environments/controls, false proof or blind native retry is used.\n\nSource-only work at capture time may include history fix, wire-format audit and NEW independent seed29 thin callers. Pending final seals, new producer/controller/index propagation, actual typed interface/science and remaining quality checks require later append. All old failures, reader/profile/preexec errors and unknowns remain; no source/CPU/model/raw/SDK/record replay for Git.\n"
